{"title":"1953 AHSME Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_14\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 14</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_14\">Problem 14</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 14\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Given the larger of two circles with center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and the smaller with center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> and radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. Draw <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/b/7ab17967324fc2b12349c0610c6c256f4c829162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />. Which of the following statements is false? \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/2/722bbadbc53597704e37865fc3630b3a4b6ad062.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ p-q\\text{ can be equal to }\\overline{PQ}\\\\  \\textbf{(B)}\\ p+q\\text{ can be equal to }\\overline{PQ}\\\\  \\textbf{(C)}\\ p+q\\text{ can be less than }\\overline{PQ}\\\\  \\textbf{(D)}\\ p-q\\text{ can be less than }\\overline{PQ}\\\\ \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{none of these}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"232\" height=\"105\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be any positive real number.  Draw a segment of length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, and label the ends <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />.  Draw a circle of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and a circle of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> centered at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />.  No matter what <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is, this is possible to do.  \n</p><p>To show that choice A can happen, use <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/d/82de6e43cae7223887882c079734ca3f2dcd61d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = p-q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"16\" />.  For choice B, use <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/e/22ece74b9aeb1dd4171c48f92b7fdaf4075a5604.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = p+q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"16\" />.  For choice C, use <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/6/e1626e56c96e7d86500134be193be4d3da97ffd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = p+q+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"106\" height=\"17\" />.  For choice D, use <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/1/aa175f02d44dac1912024b62ce7a3493f0e9e026.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = p-q+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"106\" height=\"17\" />. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/2/cc2f9302c3a9fb0d1ca271cf1572eb82fb50f4c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\text{none of these} }$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"142\" height=\"30\" /> is correct.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We will test each option to see if it can be true or not. Links to diagrams are provided.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/6/1e688d43d1c33da119b8eea5612c11048fa134f9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\textbf{(A)}\\ p-q\\text{ can be equal to }\\overline{PQ}\\]\" width=\"225\" height=\"19\" />\nLet circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> be inside circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and tangent to circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and the point of tangency be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/f/bffaf1e585a4ba16969a4fe4f2fefa9142a02546.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PR = p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"61\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/7/1871425f67706aec7790a07c5aeffb4e37af7fec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QR = q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"61\" height=\"16\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/9/9a9b24e8c5da39b859b7c0af95775ef4f188a3df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PR - QR = PQ = p-q.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"199\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/c/11c7eb7bdb195aca890838373084169544119a46.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pair P, Q, R; P = (0,0); Q = (3,0); R = (4,0); draw(Circle(P,4)); draw(Circle(Q,1)); draw(P--R); dot(P); dot(Q); dot(R); label(&quot;$P$&quot;,P,S); label(&quot;$Q$&quot;,Q,S); label(&quot;$R$&quot;,R,E); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"228\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/9/9a95d9d55e67d554764453c58f9aff43f1f4fd5f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\textbf{(B)}\\ p+q\\text{ can be equal to }\\overline{PQ}\\]\" width=\"224\" height=\"19\" />\nLet circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> be outside circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and tangent to circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and the point of tangency be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/f/bffaf1e585a4ba16969a4fe4f2fefa9142a02546.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PR = p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"61\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/7/1871425f67706aec7790a07c5aeffb4e37af7fec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QR = q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"61\" height=\"16\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/2/d128a2149bca214baa545ad515abb067b75e112b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PR + QR = PQ = p+q.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"199\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/8/ef88bf192e3f8109af9f0d810e3d13a16206f6c0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pair P, Q, R; P = (0,0); Q = (5,0); R = (4,0); draw(Circle(P,4)); draw(Circle(Q,1)); draw(P--Q); dot(P); dot(Q); dot(R); label(&quot;$P$&quot;,P,S); label(&quot;$Q$&quot;,Q,S); label(&quot;$R$&quot;,R,SW); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"202\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/2/fe2af986dceb9f4a694da53d16e915bcf6a049db.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\textbf{(C)}\\ p+q\\text{ can be less than }\\overline{PQ}\\]\" width=\"230\" height=\"19\" />\nLet circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> be outside circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and not tangent to circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/e/0deaae00f6af4ac1f5882568e7b6667bb334a2ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{PQ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"29\" height=\"19\" /> with the circles be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> respectively. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/f/bffaf1e585a4ba16969a4fe4f2fefa9142a02546.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PR = p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"61\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/f/13f84b59641e0e450605c0b56926c765e17f1fbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QS = q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"59\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/e/8befed4671e6dafc10662c2fab24d0d6345c4545.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PR + QS &lt; PQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"129\" height=\"16\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/f/31f85c450e8c86839392373f79215f3087c0c453.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p+q &lt; PQ.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"97\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/1/2114477d96aeedc200e82a28e11b3d637b51b1ec.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pair P, Q, R, SS; P = (0,0); Q = (5,0); R = (3,0); SS = (4,0); draw(Circle(P,3)); draw(Circle(Q,1)); draw(P--Q); dot(P); dot(Q); dot(R); dot(SS); label(&quot;$P$&quot;,P,S); label(&quot;$Q$&quot;,Q,S); label(&quot;$R$&quot;,R,SW); label(&quot;$S$&quot;,SS,SW); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"168\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/b/69b1f337d24bebff831aa44b88406c83002a5319.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\textbf{(D)}\\ p-q\\text{ can be less than }\\overline{PQ}\\]\" width=\"230\" height=\"19\" />\nIn the situation for choice C, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/0/f2068269293ed176870392a60c28e8cf05fe51f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p+q &lt; PQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/7/4d72f2661a24e815a6a7a00e645409e250ab06a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p-q &lt; p+q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"106\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/2/9e2eff3e0130380758f41b2cc2d87f4bd6714fb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p-q &lt; PQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"95\" height=\"18\" />.  So this is possible.\n</p><p>Since options A, B, C, and D can be true, the answer must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/2/55206bce678ac0394d97dc04dd72398df2bdf572.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{E}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"26\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME\" title=\"1953 AHSME\">1953 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1953 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1953 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1953\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1953_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1953 AHSME Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/